<div class="non-normative">

*This technical report is non-normative.*

# Introduction # {#sctn-intro}

The [[native-app-payment-handler]] API defines an abstract functional model,
the [=native payment app provider model=], through which user agents can
interact with [=native payment apps=] in order to treat them as [=native-app
payment handlers=] that are accessible via the [[payment-request]] API.

This document describes one concrete implementation of that model, the
[=Android payment app provider=], which defines how a user agent running on the
Android Operating System can interact with other applications on the same
device that want to act as payment apps.

# Android Payment App Provider # {#sctn-android-payment-app-provider}

The <dfn>Android Payment App Provider</dfn> is a [=native payment app
provider=] that defines how a user agent can access Android [=native payment
apps=]. The necessary functionality is built on top of standard Android OS
concepts for cross-application communication and collaboration:

- <a href="https://developer.android.com/guide/topics/manifest/manifest-intro">AndroidManifest.xml</a>
- <a href="https://developer.android.com/guide/topics/intents/intents-filters">Intents</a>
- <a href="https://developer.android.com/develop/background-work/services">Services</a>

## Payment app AndroidManifest.xml ## {#sctn-payment-app-android-manifest}

In order to be visible to the user agent, the Android payment app defines the
following concepts in their `AndroidManifest.xml` file:

1. An **optional** "is ready to pay" Android service, which the user agent will
     bind to and call when [[#sctn-hasenrolled-instrument|determining if the
     app can handle a PaymentRequest]].

1. A **mandatory** "pay" Android activity, which will receive an intent when
     the user agent [[#sctn-invoking|invokes the app]].

Issue: TODO add the update service

If an Android payment app specifies more than one activity or service that
matches one of the above, the user agent behavior is undefined.

### The `IS_READY_TO_PAY` service ### {#sctn-is-ready-to-pay-service}

The `IS_READY_TO_PAY` service receives calls from the user agent to
[[#sctn-hasenrolled-instrument|determine if the app can handle a
PaymentRequest]]. If present, it must be exported and have an intent filter
with an `org.chromium.intent.action.IS_READY_TO_PAY` action:

<xmp>
  <service
      ...
      android:exported="true">
    <intent-filter>
      <action android:name="org.chromium.intent.action.IS_READY_TO_PAY" />
    </intent-filter>
  </service>
</xmp>

### The `PAY` activity ### {#sctn-pay-activity}

The `PAY` activity will receive an intent from the user agent when the user
agent [[#sctn-invoking|invokes the app]] to handle a PaymentRequest. It must be
exported and have:

- An intent filter with an `org.chromium.intent.action.PAY` action
- An `org.chromium.default_payment_method_name` `<meta-data>` tag.
- Optionally, an `org.chromium.payment_method_names` `<meta-data>` tag.

The `org.chromium.default_payment_method_name` tag must be a string
representing a valid [=url-based payment method identifier=] and is used for
[[#sctn-claiming-method-url]].

<xmp>
  <activity
      ...
       android:exported="true">
    <intent-filter>
      <action android:name="org.chromium.intent.action.PAY" />
    </intent-filter>

    <meta-data
        android:name="org.chromium.default_payment_method_name"
        android:value="https://sampleapp.example/pay" />
    <meta-data
        android:name="org.chromium.payment_method_names"
        android:resource="@array/chromium_payment_method_names" />
  </activity>
</xmp>

## User agent app AndroidManifest.xml ## {#sctn-user-agent-android-manifest}

In order to be able to interact with Android [=native payment apps=], the user
agent application <a
href="https://developer.android.com/training/package-visibility/declaring">declares
its package visibility needs</a> for the relevant intent filters in its own
AndroidManifest.xml file:

<xmp>
  <queries>
    <intent>
      <action android:name="org.chromium.intent.action.PAY"/>
    </intent>
    <intent>
      <action android:name="org.chromium.intent.action.IS_READY_TO_PAY"/>
    </intent>
  </queries>
</xmp>

Issue: TODO - UPDATE_PAYMENT_DETAILS

## Returning a list of native payment apps ## {#sctn-list-native-payment-apps}

In order to [=get the list of native payment apps=], the user agent performs
the following steps:

1. Create a new Intent object, |intent|, targeting the
     `org.chromium.intent.action.PAY` action.

1. Query the Android OS for the list of activities that can be performed for
     |intent|, for example via <a href="https://developer.android.com/reference/android/content/pm/PackageManager#queryIntentActivities(android.content.Intent,%20int)">PackageManager.queryIntentActivities</a>.

1. TODO - do we need to spec how to turn the resultant info into a list of
     apps? TBD.

## Claiming a method URL ## {#sctn-claiming-method-url}

The [=claimed payment method identifier=] for an Android application, |app|, is
the value of the `org.chromium.default_payment_method_name` `<meta-data>` tag
in |app|'s AndroidManifest.xml file.

## Claiming a set of origins ## {#sctn-claiming-origins}

The [=set=] of [=claimed third-party origins=] for an Android application,
|app|, is created from the value of the `org.chromium.payment_method_names`
`<meta-data>` tag in |app|'s AndroidManifest.xml file, as follows:

1. Let |paymentMethodIdentifiers| be the value  of the `org.chromium.payment_method_names`
    `<meta-data>` tag.

1. If |paymentMethodIdentifiers| is not a string array, return an empty [=set=].

1. Let |origins| be an empty [=set=].

1. For each string |identifier| in |paymentMethodIdentifiers|:

    1. If |identifier| is not a valid [=url-based payment method identifier=],
        go to the next iteration of the loop.

    1. Let |origin| be the [=origin=] of |identifier|.

    1. Add |origin| to |origins|.

1. Return |origins|.

ISSUE: We need to document why this is an array of method URLs, rather than
just an array of origins.

## Checking if a native payment app is a related application for a web app manifest ## {#sctn-checking-related-application}

In order to check if a given Android application, |app|, [=is a related
application=] for a [=application manifest|web app manifest=], |manifest|, the
user agent performs the following steps:

1. Let |packageName| be the package name of |app|.

1. Let |version| be the version of |app|.

1. Let |fingerprint| be ...

    ISSUE: TODO - need to specify how to convert it to a string

1. For each [=related application=], |relatedApplication|, in the [=related
     applications=] of |manifest|:

    1. If |packageName| is not equal to |relatedApplication|'s [=id=], go to
        the next iteration of this loop.

    1. If |version| is less than |relatedApplication|'s [=minimum version=],
        go to the next iteration of this loop.

        ISSUE: Need to define how the comparison is done.

    1. If |fingerprint| does not match |relatedApplication|'s [=fingerprint=],
        go to the next iteration of this loop.

    1. Return `true`.

1. Return `false`.

## Determining if an Android native payment app can handle a {{PaymentRequest}} ## {#sctn-hasenrolled-instrument}

In order to check if an Android application, |app|, is [=able to handle a
payment request=], |request|, the user agent performs the following steps:

1. If |app| does not have a service listed in its AndroidManifest.xml with an
    intent-filter for `org.chromium.intent.action.IS_READY_TO_PAY` (see
    [[#sctn-is-ready-to-pay-service]]), return `false` / `true` TODO

1. If the user agent is in private browsing mode, return `false` / `true` TODO

    ISSUE: Properly link this

1. Call the IS_READY_TO_PAY service (TODO how), passing the following
     information, and wait on the result.

    1. TODO what information to pass

    ISSUE: Properly document this

1. TODO - convert the result to true/false and return that.

ISSUE: Document the privacy concerns.

## Invoking an Android native payment app ## {#sctn-invoking}

In order to [=invoke the native payment app=], |app|, for a {{PaymentRequest}}
|request|, the user agent performs the following steps:

1. Let |packageName| be the Android package name for |app|.
1. Let |activityName| be the Activity name for |app|.

     ISSUE: TODO - these name to be part of some sort of app concept

1. Let |extras| be the result of [=creating an Android bundle=] for |request|.

1. Create an Intent object, |intent|, whose:

    1. Class name is set to the combination of |packageName| and
         |activityName|, e.g. via <a href="https://developer.android.com/reference/android/content/Intent#setClassName(java.lang.String,%20java.lang.String)">Intent.setClassName</a>.

    1. Action is set to `org.chromium.intent.action.IS_READY_TO_PAY`.

    1. Extras are set to |extras|, e.g. via
         <a href="https://developer.android.com/reference/android/content/Intent#putExtras(android.os.Bundle)">Intent.putExtras</a>.

1. Send |intent| to the Android OS in such a way that the user agent will be
     notified on result, e.g. via <a href="https://developer.android.com/reference/android/app/Activity#startActivityForResult(android.content.Intent,%20int)">Activity.startActivityForResult</a>.

